SUMMARY:The Saturday Night Autumn Mix and Mingle Dinner Party! 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nGood day everyone\,\n\nJoin us for
  a fun and relaxed Saturday night of good food\, great conversation and ne
 w connections! Come on your own or bring a friend and enjoy an easygoing a
 utumn evening with new and old friends alike.\n\n\\*Joined by my other soc
 ial groups too\; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out with lots of fri
 endly peers to begin our weekend with!\n\n\\*Please note we are at **The P
 heasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Law
 rence - south of the 401 **(we are in the back dining area or on the patio
 \, depending on weather and numbers)**\n\n*\\*You can ask the bartender if
  you like to show you to the group (simply ask for Steve's dinner party)*\
 n\n-You'll find it's a cozy\, relaxed and enjoyable atmosphere!\n\n**-Free
  Parking found on residential side streets**\n\n(Event Details Below)\n\nS
 incerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host )\n\nEvent Details:\n**🎉*
 * **The Saturday Night Autumn Mix and Mingle Dinner Party**\n**(Saturday\,
  September 26th\, 2026)**\n\nWe’re getting together at The Pheasant on A
 venue Road for our **Saturday Night Autumn Mix and Mingle Dinner Party!**\
 nThis is a casual social evening where you can enjoy dinner and drinks whi
 le meeting new people in a comfortable and friendly atmosphere. Whether yo
 u're new to the group or one of our regulars\, you're very welcome to join
  us.\n\n• 🍽️ Enjoy dinner and drinks\n• 🍂 Relaxed autumn socia
 l atmosphere\n• 👋 Meet new people and make new friends\n• 💬 Plen
 ty of time to mix\, mingle and chat\n• 👫 Singles\, couples and friend
 s are all welcome\n• 😊 Come alone — many of our members do!\n\nLook
 ing forward to another enjoyable Saturday night together!\nHosted by Steve
  Flemming (Soul City Social Club)\n\n**Event Fee:** 10 dollars (Cash only 
 at the door) (HST included)\nor by e transfer: **steveflemming11@gmail.com
 **\n\\*No extra charge for those attending the 3 pm walk :)\n\\*No extra c
 harge if you are staying for Karaoke as well\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\
 n-Arrive any time between 6:00 pm and 7:00 pm (please ask for Steve when y
 ou arrive\n\n\\*Great dinner menu and food specials provided:\n\n**Parking
  and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free resid
 ential parking\nhttps://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/\n\n(15-20
  minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or ub
 er from the station)
